    scratch word built by draw_dungeon_monster as (monsters_ptr_hi : _dungeonMonsterBandOffsets[di]) -- i.e. the absolute address of the current depth band's 2-byte marker record inside the MONSTERS buffer. Read twice: once for the X byte, once (incremented) for the packed Y/facing byte. Formerly word_17899.
1788F: 'byte_1788F' -> '_dungeonMonsterFacing'
    top 3 bits of the MONSTERS record's second byte (extracted via 5x `clc`+`rcr al,1`, equivalent to `>> 5`) -- a 0-7 facing/type value selecting which pixel pattern draw_sprite_row draws for the monster marker at this depth. Written by draw_dungeon_monster, read by draw_dungeon_monster_sprite. Formerly byte_1788F.
